-- What staff and the AI are told of a year's rent increase capped by inflation, from the first
-- of March 2027, the notice going out on 11/15/2026 (src/pms/rent_cap.py, renewals.limit_for;
-- docs/law.md). Five homes of one company, each a month-to-month lease at 1000.00:
--   Los Angeles area (CA, ZIP 90000): April 2025 300.000 to April 2026 309.000, 3.0%: at most
--     8.0% over 1000.00, 1080.00; 1100.00 asked is over it.
--   San Diego area (CA, ZIP 92100): no April, so March 2025 300.000 to March 2026 312.000, 4.0%:
--     at most 9.0%, 1090.00; 1050.00 asked is within it.
--   Elsewhere in California (ZIP 95800): no BLS area the PMS can place: at most 10%, 1100.00;
--     1120.00 asked is over it.
--   Oregon (ZIP 97000): rent 1030.00 from 09/01/2026 (once in 12 months, said); the West Region
--     at 300 + 0.5 a month from October 2024: 302.750 then 308.750 a year on average, 2.0%: at
--     most 9.0% over the rent now, 1030.00, 1122.70; 1100.00 asked is within it.
--   Washington (ZIP 98000): its tenants came 09/01/2026 (no increase in the first 12 months,
--     said); Seattle June 2025 300.000 to June 2026 308.049, 2.683%: at most 9.683%, 1096.83;
--     1080.00 asked is within it.
-- Every ZIP code is one USPS never issued, of a prefix the PMS reads; every figure is made up.

